1
00:00:00,559 --> 00:00:05,719
him to take care of his health, but Boxer paid no attention.

2
00:00:05,719 --> 00:00:10,959
His 12th birthday was approaching. He did not care what happened, so long as a

3
00:00:10,959 --> 00:00:17,120
good store of stone was accumulated before he went on pension.

4
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:21,959
Late one evening in the summer, a sudden rumor ran round the farm that something

5
00:00:21,959 --> 00:00:24,319
had happened to Boxer.

6
00:00:24,319 --> 00:00:28,440
He had gone out alone to drag a load of stone down to the windmill,

7
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:31,719
and sure enough, the rumor was true.

8
00:00:31,719 --> 00:00:36,239
A few minutes later, two pigeons came racing in with the news.

9
00:00:36,239 --> 00:00:40,799
>> Boxer has fallen. He is lying on his side and can't get up.

10
00:00:40,799 --> 00:00:45,680
>> About half the animals on the farm rushed out to the knoll where the windmill stood.

11
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:51,719
There lay Boxer between the shafts of the cart, his neck stretched out, unable

12
00:00:51,719 --> 00:00:54,120
even to raise his head.

13
00:00:54,120 --> 00:00:58,959
His eyes were glazed, his sides matted with sweat.

14
00:00:58,959 --> 00:01:03,000
A thin stream of blood had trickled out of his mouth.

15
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:06,040
Clover drops to her knees at his side.

16
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:08,920
>> Boxer, how are you?

17
00:01:08,920 --> 00:01:11,040
>> It is my lung.

18
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:12,959
It does not matter.

19
00:01:12,959 --> 00:01:16,399
I think you will be able to finish the windmill without me.

20
00:01:16,399 --> 00:01:19,200
There is a pretty good store of stone accumulated.

21
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:22,159
I had only another month to go in any case.

22
00:01:22,159 --> 00:01:26,239
To tell you the truth, I had been looking forward to my retirement,

23
00:01:26,239 --> 00:01:30,840
and perhaps, as Benjamin is growing old, too, they will let him retire at the

24
00:01:30,840 --> 00:01:34,840
same time and be a companion to me.

25
00:01:35,079 --> 00:01:40,559
>> We must get help at once. Run, somebody, and tell Squealer what has happened.

26
00:01:40,559 --> 00:01:46,239
>> All the other animals immediately raced back to the farmhouse to give Squealer the news.

27
00:01:46,239 --> 00:01:52,280
Only Clover remained, and Benjamin, who lay down at Boxer's side, and without

28
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:57,200
speaking, kept the flies off him with his long tail.

29
00:01:57,200 --> 00:02:03,360
After about a quarter of an hour, Squealer appeared, full of sympathy and concern.

30
00:02:03,360 --> 00:02:08,040
He said that Comrade Napoleon had learned with the very deepest distress

31
00:02:08,040 --> 00:02:12,520
of this misfortune to one of the most loyal workers on the farm

32
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:19,280
and was already making arrangements to send Boxer to be treated in the hospital at Willingdon.

33
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:22,559
The animals felt a little uneasy at this.

34
00:02:22,559 --> 00:02:28,440
Except for Mollie and Snowball, no other animal had ever left the farm

35
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:34,280
and they did not like to think of their sick comrade in the hands of human beings.

36
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:38,520
However, Squealer easily convinced them that the veterinary surgeon in

37
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:44,760
Willingdon could treat Boxer's case more satisfactorily than could be done on the farm.

38
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:50,079
And about half an hour later, when Boxer had somewhat recovered, he was, with

39
00:02:50,079 --> 00:02:55,399
difficulty, got onto his feet and managed to limp back to his stall, where

40
00:02:55,399 --> 00:03:00,000
Clover and Benjamin had prepared a good bed of straw for him.

41
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:05,040
For the next two days, Boxer remained in his stall. The pigs had sent out a large

42
00:03:05,040 --> 00:03:09,639
bottle of pink medicine, which they had found in the medicine chest in the bathroom,

43
00:03:09,639 --> 00:03:14,200
and Clover administered it to Boxer twice a day after meals.

44
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:19,079
In the evenings, she lay in his stall and talked to him, while Benjamin kept

45
00:03:19,079 --> 00:03:21,000
the flies off him.

46
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,799
Boxer professed not to be sorry for what had happened.

47
00:03:24,799 --> 00:03:29,239
If he made a good recovery, he might expect to live another three years and

48
00:03:29,239 --> 00:03:34,760
he looked forward to the peaceful days that he would spend in the corner of the big pasture.

49
00:03:34,760 --> 00:03:40,280
It would be the first time that he had had leisure to study and improve his mind.

50
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:46,079
He intended, he said, to devote the rest of his life to learning the remaining 22

51
00:03:46,079 --> 00:03:48,200
letters of the alphabet.

52
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:53,680
However, Benjamin and Clover could only be with Boxer after working hours and it

53
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:58,280
was in the middle of the day when the van came to take him away.

54
00:03:58,280 --> 00:04:03,000
The animals were all at work weeding turnips under the supervision of a pig

55
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:06,000
when they were astonished to see Benjamin come galloping from the
